# The integration trains' working logs (merge tooling, per-merge counts, ctest
# and gate logs). Working material, not product content: Gate 6 classifies every
# changed path, and a log directory at the repository root has no class it
# allows. The three earlier trains' directories were already untracked; the
# wave-4 train committed its own by accident, and the 2026-09-15 wave-5 train
# untracked it (files kept on disk) and moved its RECORD to
# docs/reports/MERGE-TRAIN-030w4.md. Keep them out of git.
/.merge-logs-*/

# (The tests/integration-logs-ci-fix/**/out/ ignore rule that stood here was removed with
# the committed evidence on 2026-09-13, REPO-1/CP-1: the harness directory it covered is
# gone, and an ignore rule for a path that no longer exists only hides a future reuse of
# the name. tests/evidence-manifest.tsv records what was removed and its hashes.)

# The 030/session-api-proof lane's proof scratch directories (2026-09-15): .proof-bin
# holds the copy of the wave-4 train's linked binary its transcript was measured
# against, .proof-ctest the configure-only tree the ctest registration was read out
# of. Both are working material rather than product content, and only their
# .gitignore files were committed — which Gate 6 has no class for (its build/config
# rule admits the ROOT .gitignore, and its docs rule admits *.md). Untracked at the
# wave-9 merge for the same reason as the /.merge-logs-*/ block above: the files stay
# on disk, the directories are recorded in docs/reports/SESSION-API-PROOF-2026-09-15.md,
# and neither is a candidate for any scope manifest (those admit source extensions).
/.proof-bin/
/.proof-ctest/
